; XSparkFlow - XAUUSD M30 CandleFlow, the recommended starting configuration
;
; This file simply writes down the settings the EA already defaults to, so you
; can see them in one place and diff them against anything you change. Loading
; it on a fresh chart changes nothing.
;
; It is a STARTING POINT, not a validated profile: CandleFlow has never been
; backtested, forward-tested or traded. Nothing here is a profitability claim.
;
; WHAT THE BOT DOES
;   A 30-minute candle finishes higher than it started  -> it buys.
;   A 30-minute candle finishes lower than it started   -> it sells.
;   It banks 30% of the trade once it is 1.5 times the amount risked in
;   front, and another 30% at 3 times. The remaining 40% has no target and
;   ends when its stop-loss is hit.
;   The stop only ever moves in your favour, never away.
;
; WHY IT BANKS PROFIT IN STEPS
;   A trailing stop can only act after the price has come back by the whole
;   trail distance, so a trade that runs a long way and then turns around is
;   closed well below the best price it saw. The two steps take most of that
;   move off the table before the turn can reach it, and the 40% that is left
;   keeps the open-ended upside the rule exists for.
;
;   Set InpFlowTP1AtR and InpFlowTP2AtR to 0 to get the original behaviour,
;   where the trailing stop is the only exit. xauusd-m30-candleflow-no-targets.set
;   is exactly this file with those levels off, and is the one-change A/B for
;   "did the levels help". Run it ON REAL TICKS: the levels trigger on a
;   tick-resolution price while the trailing stop only advances on finished
;   candles, so low-resolution modelling understates them.
;
;   A step needs enough lots to be legal: it must close at least the broker's
;   minimum and leave at least that much behind. On a 0.01 minimum a two-step
;   ladder needs about 0.03 lots. Below that the steps are skipped, logged
;   once, and the trade simply runs on its trailing stop.
;
; HOW THE STOP MOVES, in plain terms
;   It starts just past the signal candle's far end.
;   It follows 3 candle-heights behind the best price the trade has seen.
;   Once the trade is up more than it risked, it tightens towards 1.5, and
;   your entry price is protected so the trade can no longer become a loss.
;   It is never parked closer than 0.35 candle-heights to the live price,
;   because a stop inside the spread is just a slow market order.
;
; TO CHANGE TIMEFRAME: attach the EA to a different chart period. Every distance
; here is a multiple of that period's own candle size or of the amount risked on
; the trade, so nothing in this file needs editing.
;
; Trading is DISABLED. Turn InpFlowEnableTrading on only after a Strategy Tester
; run and a demo account have shown you what this actually does - it is in the
; market far more often than ScoreBot_v3.

InpFlowEnableTrading=false
InpFlowAutoTuneForSymbol=true
InpFlowMaxOpenTrades=1

InpFlowMinBodyATRMult=0.0

InpFlowBufferATRMult=0.10
InpFlowBufferRangePct=0.0
InpFlowBufferPoints=0.0
InpFlowMinStopATRMult=0.25
InpFlowMaxStopATRMult=0.0

InpFlowMinTrailATRMult=0.35
InpFlowTrailATRMult=3.0
InpFlowTrailTightATRMult=1.5
InpFlowTrailTightenStartR=1.0
InpFlowTrailTightenFullR=4.0
InpFlowBreakevenAtR=1.2
InpFlowBreakevenOffsetR=0.1

InpFlowTP1AtR=1.5
InpFlowTP1ClosePct=30.0
InpFlowTP2AtR=3.0
InpFlowTP2ClosePct=30.0
InpFlowTP3AtR=0.0
InpFlowTP3ClosePct=0.0
InpFlowFinalTargetR=0.0

InpFlowRiskPct=1.0
InpFlowMaxRiskPct=3.5
InpFlowMaxAccountRiskPct=6.0
InpFlowMaxDailyDDPct=15.0
InpFlowUseTotalDDKillSwitch=true
InpFlowMaxTotalDDPct=25.0

InpFlowUseWeekendClose=true
InpFlowWeekendCloseHour=20
InpFlowWeekendCloseMinute=0

InpFlowVerboseLog=false

InpFlowUseVolatilityGate=false

InpFlowQuietMarketPct=60.0
InpFlowWildMarketPct=600.0
InpFlowEntrySlipPct=25.0
InpFlowExitSlipPct=85.0
InpFlowSpreadCapPct=40.0
InpFlowMaxSpreadATRPct=10.0

InpFlowUseSpreadFilter=true
InpFlowUseStopLevelValidation=true
InpFlowUseMarginCheck=true
InpFlowMarginBufferPct=20.0
InpFlowMaxQuoteAgeSeconds=15

InpFlowMagicNumber=770332
InpFlowOrderComment=CandleFlow_v1
InpFlowClearKillswitchLatch=false
